      "writtenOn": "2025-02-15T02:45:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sigh, the same true/false block is annoying. We can endup seeing the same SPIR-V ID multiple times, which goes to different values. So, probalby I just need to make it update the SPIR-V ID, although that in itself is kinda weird.\n\nI wonder if the better solution to same true/false block is to just, change it to something like:\n\n```\nif (true || \u003coriginal condition\u003e) {\n   \u003cemit block\u003e\n}\n```\n\nSo we still have a usage of original condition, but we always force it down the true block and only emit once.",
      "parentUuid": "36193e4e_2fc8a477",
      "revId": "79c039d251871e99f359451291fed28c5792c9c2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
