      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure I\u0027m following, the source instruction block may not be in the block stack. If it\u0027s in a block we\u0027ve already popped from the stack, then it wouldn\u0027t be found.\n\nThis is the path from the source instruction up to the function.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\nfn a() {\n  if (b) {\n    %1 \u003d 4;\n  }\n  \n  %2 \u003d %1\n}\n```\n\nThe block containing %1 isn\u0027t on the block stack anymore because we\u0027ve exited it, but we still need to look it up to hoist.",
